('page fault Use Case', 'When should you use page fault while solving Memory Management problems?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'OPERATING_SYSTEM', 'Memory Management', '["Use it to bring needed pages into memory on demand","Use it only after the program has already terminated","Use it to avoid defining clear input and output boundaries","Use it when correctness does not depend on state or ordering"]', 'Use it to bring needed pages into memory on demand'),
('page fault Pitfall', 'Which mistake is most closely related to page fault?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'OPERATING_SYSTEM', 'Memory Management', '["Treating every page fault as a fatal application error","Assuming it always has zero cost and no side effects","Using it without checking whether the input data matches the assumption","Treating all implementations as identical in every database or operating system"]', 'Treating every page fault as a fatal application error'),
('page fault Example', 'Which example correctly demonstrates page fault?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'OPERATING_SYSTEM', 'Memory Management', '["The OS handles a minor page fault by updating the page table","A comment that says the code is correct","A variable name chosen because it looks readable","A command or query that does not reference the concept"]', 'The OS handles a minor page fault by updating the page table'),
