('LRU replacement Use Case', 'When should you use LRU replacement while solving Memory Management problems?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'OPERATING_SYSTEM', 'Memory Management', '["Use it as an approximation of locality-based page replacement","Use it only after the program has already terminated","Use it to avoid defining clear input and output boundaries","Use it when correctness does not depend on state or ordering"]', 'Use it as an approximation of locality-based page replacement'),
('LRU replacement Pitfall', 'Which mistake is most closely related to LRU replacement?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'OPERATING_SYSTEM', 'Memory Management', '["Assuming exact LRU is always cheap to implement in hardware","Assuming it always has zero cost and no side effects","Using it without checking whether the input data matches the assumption","Treating all implementations as identical in every database or operating system"]', 'Assuming exact LRU is always cheap to implement in hardware'),
('LRU replacement Example', 'Which example correctly demonstrates LRU replacement?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'OPERATING_SYSTEM', 'Memory Management', '["The page not accessed for the longest time is replaced","A comment that says the code is correct","A variable name chosen because it looks readable","A command or query that does not reference the concept"]', 'The page not accessed for the longest time is replaced'),
('Clock algorithm Meaning', 'In Memory Management (MEDIUM), which statement best describes Clock algorithm?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'OPERATING_SYSTEM', 'Memory Management', '["A second-chance page replacement algorithm using a circular pointer and reference bits","It is only a visual formatting convention and has no runtime meaning","It is a compiler-only feature that never affects execution","It is used only for documentation and cannot change program behavior"]', 'A second-chance page replacement algorithm using a circular pointer and reference bits'),
('Clock algorithm Use Case', 'When should you use Clock algorithm while solving Memory Management problems?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'OPERATING_SYSTEM', 'Memory Management', '["Use it as an efficient approximation of LRU","Use it only after the program has already terminated","Use it to avoid defining clear input and output boundaries","Use it when correctness does not depend on state or ordering"]', 'Use it as an efficient approximation of LRU'),
