('DISTINCT Example', 'Which example correctly demonstrates DISTINCT?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'DBMS', 'SQL Basics', '["SELECT DISTINCT city FROM Customers;","A comment that says the code is correct","A variable name chosen because it looks readable","A command or query that does not reference the concept"]', 'SELECT DISTINCT city FROM Customers;'),
('aggregate functions Meaning', 'In SQL Basics (MEDIUM), which statement best describes aggregate functions?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'DBMS', 'SQL Basics', '["Functions such as COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, and MAX that summarize rows","It is only a visual formatting convention and has no runtime meaning","It is a compiler-only feature that never affects execution","It is used only for documentation and cannot change program behavior"]', 'Functions such as COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, and MAX that summarize rows'),
('aggregate functions Use Case', 'When should you use aggregate functions while solving SQL Basics problems?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'DBMS', 'SQL Basics', '["Use them to compute summary metrics over rows or groups","Use it only after the program has already terminated","Use it to avoid defining clear input and output boundaries","Use it when correctness does not depend on state or ordering"]', 'Use them to compute summary metrics over rows or groups'),
('aggregate functions Pitfall', 'Which mistake is most closely related to aggregate functions?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'DBMS', 'SQL Basics', '["Forgetting that COUNT(column) ignores NULL values","Assuming it always has zero cost and no side effects","Using it without checking whether the input data matches the assumption","Treating all implementations as identical in every database or operating system"]', 'Forgetting that COUNT(column) ignores NULL values'),
('aggregate functions Example', 'Which example correctly demonstrates aggregate functions?', 'MCQ', 'MEDIUM', 'DBMS', 'SQL Basics', '["SELECT COUNT(*), AVG(salary) FROM Employees;","A comment that says the code is correct","A variable name chosen because it looks readable","A command or query that does not reference the concept"]', 'SELECT COUNT(*), AVG(salary) FROM Employees;'),
