('2NF Pitfall', 'Which mistake is most closely related to 2NF?', 'MCQ', 'EASY', 'DBMS', 'Normalization', '["Keeping an attribute that depends on only part of a composite key","Assuming it always has zero cost and no side effects","Using it without checking whether the input data matches the assumption","Treating all implementations as identical in every database or operating system"]', 'Keeping an attribute that depends on only part of a composite key'),
('2NF Example', 'Which example correctly demonstrates 2NF?', 'MCQ', 'EASY', 'DBMS', 'Normalization', '["In Enrollment(student_id, course_id, course_name), course_name depends only on course_id","A comment that says the code is correct","A variable name chosen because it looks readable","A command or query that does not reference the concept"]', 'In Enrollment(student_id, course_id, course_name), course_name depends only on course_id'),
('3NF Meaning', 'In Normalization (EASY), which statement best describes 3NF?', 'MCQ', 'EASY', 'DBMS', 'Normalization', '["A normal form where non-key attributes do not depend on other non-key attributes","It is only a visual formatting convention and has no runtime meaning","It is a compiler-only feature that never affects execution","It is used only for documentation and cannot change program behavior"]', 'A normal form where non-key attributes do not depend on other non-key attributes'),
